  "final_answer": "### Step 4: Calculate `pay_per_use_total`\nThe `pay_per_use_total` is calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{pay\\_per\\_use\\_total} = 1000 \\times 1.00 + 500 \\times 0.19 + 300 \\times 0.49 = 1000 + 95 + 147 = 1242.0 \\]\n\n### Step 5: Calculate `membership_total`\nThe `membership_total` is calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{membership\\_total} = 12 \\times 29.00 + 100 \\times 0.17 + 300 \\times 0.17 = 348.00 + 17.00 + 51.00 = 416.00 \\]\n\n### Step 6: Calculate `break_even_rides_per_month`\nThe `break_even_rides_per_month` is calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{break\\_even\\_rides\\_per\\_month} = \\frac{29.00}{\\left(\\frac{1242.00}{1000}\\right)} = \\frac{29.00}{1.242} \\approx 23.38 \\]\n\n### Decision\nSince `membership_total` (416.00) is greater than `pay_per_use_total` (1242.00), the rider should choose the \"Pay Per Ride/Minute\" option.\n\n### Final Answer\nDecision: Pay Per Ride/Minute\nJustification: The cost of the monthly membership (416.00) is higher than the cost of paying per ride (1242.00). The break-even point is approximately 23.38 rides per month, meaning the rider would save money by paying per ride/minute for rides less than 23.38 rides per month. The pricing passages from the policy_retriever tool confirm the single ride and month pass prices for both classic and ebike riders.",
